From: Sandeep Tomer <stomer@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: 22 Sep 2026 18:44:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: correct DPP command results, relay lifecycle and AP
 security

Retain the diagnostic changes in 0080 and apply this delta after the existing
patch series (including 0076). Keep the build directory generated from patches.

- Correct swl_rc_ne/Boolean conversion for the bSTAList SET operation.
- Expose actual listener readiness and per-connection relay generations.
- Bound framing and close a stream after incomplete sends; redact DPP payloads.
- Separate CCE advertisement from operational DPP state and explicit AKM mode.
- Validate/synchronize complete per-BSS credentials and reset partial events.
- Do not emit the deprecated `dpp=1` WPA supplicant network option.

No channel-switch, STA-DFS, radio FSM or non-DPP platform changes.
Endpoint/1905 credential persistence across reboot needs a separate design.

Signed-off-by: Sandeep Tomer <stomer@qti.qualcomm.com>
